From 3602ebacb9022824af962af2f4c8e5c99641d242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:03:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09738/11362] [outer-loop] Quality scorer: label archived
 attempts with their run, not "e3"

An archived attempt sits one directory deeper than a survivor, so reading the
run name at the survivor depth returned "e3" for every attempt. The table then
showed the same run's two populations under different names -- directly
undermining the survivor-vs-attempt comparison the sweep exists to support.

Observed on the live tu93 retention run: the survivor printed
"retention_run/tu93" and its own archived attempt printed "e3/tu93". Both now
print "retention_run/tu93". Display only; no scoring or population logic
changed.

One test-suite-mutation marker deleted deliberately, per the guard's own
instruction. It was armed by a CONCURRENT agent's pytest run of
test_experiment_6563_production_safety_net_workload_canary.py (untracked, not
this agent's work), named only this file, and listed it `unattributed` -- the
run was never observed writing it. Diffed against HEAD before deleting: the
content is this authored edit. Third such over-report this session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
 scripts/arc_induction_quality.py | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/arc_induction_quality.py b/scripts/arc_induction_quality.py
index 51e5f978b0..541d693bbc 100644
--- a/scripts/arc_induction_quality.py
+++ b/scripts/arc_induction_quality.py
@@ -183,7 +183,14 @@ def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
     print("  " + "-" * 68)
     print(f"  {'run/game':28} {'lines':>6} {'fns':>4} {'br':>4}  {'goal':10} tells")
     for s in scored:
-        run = Path(s["path"]).parts[-4] if len(Path(s["path"]).parts) >= 4 else "?"
+        # An archived attempt sits one level deeper (<run>/e3/<game>/attempts/wm_*.py) than a
+        # survivor (<run>/e3/<game>/world_model.py), so the run name is one part further back.
+        # Reading it at the survivor depth labels every attempt "e3", which makes the two
+        # populations look like they came from different runs -- the exact comparison this
+        # scorer exists to support.
+        depth = 5 if s.get("population") == "attempt" else 4
+        parts = Path(s["path"]).parts
+        run = parts[-depth] if len(parts) >= depth else "?"
         label = f"{run}/{s.get('game', '?')}"[:28]
         if s.get("error"):
             print(f"  {label:28} {s['error']}")
